      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 1,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "SDR to HDR",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "1. Pick an 8-bit image or video in Read.\n2. SDR to HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2, the learned ACES 2.0 model (Apache 2.0, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run). The result is a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the source codes; reconstructed_mask shows where light was estimated.\n3. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 with the SDR source as compare_image: use the wipe to see what changed.\n4. Write saves a 32-bit float EXR. Set output_path and filename to taste.\n\nFor large blown highlights, add SDR to HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) after Universal (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU). The report output says which model ran."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "1. Pick an 8-bit image or video in Read.\n2. SDR to HDR Universal runs RUDRA ACES 2, the learned ACES 2.0 model (Apache 2.0, about 3 MB, downloaded on first run). The result is a scene-linear master (1.0 = 203 nits) whose ACES 2.0 SDR view keeps the source codes; reconstructed_mask shows where light was estimated.\n3. The Viewer shows the master through ACES 2.0 with the SDR source as compare_image: use the wipe to see what changed.\n4. Write saves a 32-bit float EXR. Set output_path and filename to taste.\n\nFor large blown highlights, add SDR to HDR AI Fill (RUDRA v3) after Universal (needs Wan2.1-VACE-1.3B and a 16 GB GPU). The report output says which model ran."
      },
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    }
